{"id": "haiku__GEN__omni_405__1", "result": "Let $a = 2001^{1002}$, so $a^{-1} = 2001^{-1002}$.\n\nThen\n$$x = a - a^{-1}, \\qquad y = a + a^{-1}.$$\n\nSquaring each:\n$$x^2 = a^2 - 2 + a^{-2}, \\qquad y^2 = a^2 + 2 + a^{-2}.$$\n\nSubtracting:\n$$x^2 - y^2 = (a^2 - 2 + a^{-2}) - (a^2 + 2 + a^{-2}) = -4.$$\n\nAs a check, $x^2 - y^2 = (x-y)(x+y) = (-2a^{-1})(2a) = -4$.\n\nANSWER: -4", "rc": 0, "cost": 0.00035039, "model_used": ["claude-haiku-5-5"], "secs": 4.6}